  "correct_answer": "27",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the wavelength of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>-line in Balmer series is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the wavelength of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub></math>-line in Balmer series is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide equation (2) by equation (1)&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
